{"title":"2019 MPFG Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_MPFG_Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a right prism whose two bases are equilateral triangles with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the line connecting the centroids of the bases. Remove the solid, keeping only the bases. Rotate one of the bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the convex hull of the two current triangles. What is the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_MPFG_Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is a demonstration of the actual transformation\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2019MPFG_17.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6b/2019MPFG_17.jpg/450px-2019MPFG_17.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"316\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6b/2019MPFG_17.jpg/675px-2019MPFG_17.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6b/2019MPFG_17.jpg/900px-2019MPFG_17.jpg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>As we can see, the transformation creates a rectangular prism with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangular pyramids cut off from the corners.\n</p><p>The volume of the rectangular prism is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729378ba76c799ca473156217c6cec824426c415.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\cdot (2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} = 12\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Subtract the volume of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangular pyramids, and we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d094512789de79b27e7ed2695578d2f9b3657530.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = 12 - 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot (2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403f643c2e93b50c95b4fc663d020315a913cab0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 12 - 8 = \\boxed{4}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~cassphe\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062559\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 65/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2455/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33570:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062559 and revision id 266895. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}